 "text": "Parks Department - Cape Girardeau County\nSkip to Content Site map\nCounty Home\nContact Parks\nParks Home\nCompare Parks Shelters\nReserve a Park Shelter\nCart\nLog In\nMy Account\nContact Parks\nParks Home\nCompare Parks Shelters\nReserve a Park Shelter\nCart\nLog In\nMy Account\nContact Parks\nHome\nCounty Offices\nAdvisory Boards\nCounty Resources County News\nCounty Purchasing Information\nCalendar of Events\nHomestead Tax Credit\nFrequently Asked Questions\nBudgetary Info\nCounty Parcel Map Viewer\nElection Information\nEmployment Opportunities\nSearch\nSearch\nParks Department\nHome Parks Department\nSearch\nCounty Parks Parks Department\nReserve a Park Shelter\nContact the Parks Department\nCompare Parks Shelters\nCape County Park Rules and Regulations\nParks Department FAQ\nHoliday of Lights Display\nBryan Sander, Park Superintendent\nLocation:\n2400 County Park Dr.\nCape Girardeau, MO 63701\nPhone: 573-335-4146\nOffice Hours: 8:00 AM – 4:00 PM\nMonday through Friday\nDeclaring America’s freedom is a 20’ X 30’ American flag towering daily over the hills of Cape County Park. An inspirational avenue of over 800 flags fly on Memorial Day, Independence Day and Veterans Day at the entrance to North Park. Each flag bears the name of a Cape County veteran.\nAvenue of Flags history.\nReserve a Park Shelter online\nPay for Holiday of Lights Display Online\nThe new website includes information regarding each park shelter, availability of each shelter, and the ability to reserve a shelter in real-time using a valid credit card. Contact us at 573-335-4146 if assistance is needed.\nCape County Park is comprised of:\nNorth Park\nSouth Park\nKlaus Park\nPark hours: 6:30 AM – 10:00 PM Daily\nMission Statement\nThe purpose of the Cape Girardeau County Park Department is to perpetuate, conserve, manage, and enhance Cape Girardeau County’s parks and outdoor recreational opportunities for the use, benefit, and enjoyment of the people of this county and its visitors, and to give the highest priority to the welfare of this county’s parks and their environment, in planning and decisions.\nHoliday of Lights Display\nFrequently Asked Questions About Cape County Parks\nStay Connected\n\" * \" indicates required fields\nYour Name *\nEmail Address *\nSubmit\nCape Girardeau County\n#1 Barton Square, Jackson, MO 63755\nMon - Fri: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n+1 573 204 2494\nQuick Links\nHome\nAdvisory Boards\nCounty Offices\nContact Us\nTransparency in Coverage\nCounty Resources\nBudgetary Info\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\nEmployment Opportunities\nCounty Purchasing Information\nCopyright © 2026 Cape Girardeau County. All Rights Reserved. Accessibility\nPowered by B&B Media\nNotifications",
